<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrés de Santa Cruz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1792">1792</a>–<a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrés de Santa Cruz was President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> from 1829 to 1839. In 1836 he joined Bolivia with the North and South Peruvian republics in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>–Bolivian Confederation, taking the title of Supreme Protector. Chile and Argentine forces opposed it, and after his defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yungay">Battle of Yungay</a> in 1839 the confederation was dissolved and he went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz.jpg" alt="Andrés de Santa Cruz" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manuel Ugalde · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andr%C3%A9s_de_Santa_Cruz._Ugalde,_Manuel._c._1835,_Andr%C3%A9s_de_Santa_Cruz_collection,_La_Paz.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
